Hi David,

We matched all four of Tuesday's confirmed absences to Session 8 and the Prin=
t allowance exercise (HO-009 v1.0) on 29 October. Three learners received bot=
h pages by the end of Wednesday, 30 October.

The fourth case, T04, was the large-print copy with page 2 missing. Kathleen =
passed the outstanding work to Arjun on Tuesday, and he confirmed at 16:12 th=
at he'd taken it on. We held back the single-page copy on Wednesday because t=
he learner needed the worked answers on page 2 to check both decisions indepe=
ndently. The learner received both pages of v1.0 at 10:20 this morning, a day=
 after the deadline.

In Monday's practice we had to read the handoff back a second time after the =
sender wrote in the receipt time. We'll keep Arjun's confirmation as the hand=
off time and record delivery when the complete exercise reaches the learner. =
For the next duty, we'll also keep the page check on the desk handoff so whoe=
ver prepares a paper copy checks every page against the matched version befor=
e it goes out, including the answer page.

I've attached the review and a separate workbook with the four cases and thei=
r delivery times.

Thanks,
Heather

